        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 80-year-old male patient, admitted on 17/05/2010 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, physical examination revealed decreased breath sounds bilaterally with prolonged expiration and audible wheezing. Oxygen saturation was reduced at 88% on room air. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxemic respiratory failure with mild hypercapnia. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without signs of pneumonia or cardiac decompensation. Blood tests demonstrated a mild inflammatory response. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulized bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Clinical condition improved satisfactorily and the patient was discharged on 18/05/2010 in stable condition. Please ensure continued outpatient follow-up and optimization of his maintenance inhaler therapy. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
